2	
3	## Crate Root (`michi`)
4	
5	`michi` is a unified facade crate. It re-exports sub-crates as modules and star-exports `michi-core` directly so all core types are available at the root:
6	
7	```rust
8	pub use michi_core::*;            // DomainError, AgentResponse, KvItem, … at michi::*
9	pub use michi_resilience as resilience;   // michi::resilience::RetryConfig, …
10	pub use michi_toon as toon;              // michi::toon::ToonOptions, michi::toon::list(), …
11	pub use michi_truncate as truncate;      // michi::truncate::truncate(), …
12	```
13	
14	`michi_resilience::*` is also re-exported from `michi_core`, so `michi::RetryConfig`, `michi::already_done`, etc. are available at the root without the `resilience::` prefix.
15	
16	All sub-crates compile for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` and `wasm32-wasip1` without OS dependencies.
17	
18	## `michi-toon` — List Rendering
19	
20	`michi-toon` formats tabular lists using Token-Optimized Object Notation (**AXI P1**). Small cell strings (≤ 24 bytes) are stack-inlined via `compact_str::CompactString`.
